Z||000033||theogre||10-21-2001||03:10 PM||||Some people have animated gifs, including one made of a fiero passing on the highway.... Yup...<P>Animation in and of itself isn't the problem here. File size of both animated and static images is a major problem. SIGs have to be kept small or the whole system slows. Even when viewed on T3 and OC96 pipes. Add a bunch of fat sigs to even fatter images some people are putting in the body and it can take several minutes to load a page, especially when images are pulled from third party sites like Photopoint etc.<P>The one of the passing car was actively discussed and reworked and used in acordance with that discussion. It's not full motion. It's actually an animated GIF as I recall. It's usually used only once per thread from what I've seen. It's also not a comercial link.<P>Recently I've use the animated flags that clif provided, but, same thing, I try to only use it once per thread and I'm not linking to comercial sites.<P>Your animation crossed a line with allot of people, you guessed it, because it's an obvious commercial banner. You however ARE NOT the only person who has been asked to rework links and images in sigs for one or more reasons. There have been multiple announcements and discussions about SIGs that have mainly gone ignored by many people. This is anything but a new issue.<P>You say you were joking about the castrated line.... It went over like jokes about Anthrax. Such jokes have resulted in Immediate termination of employment for some people. If you remark was a joke, it was in extremely poor taste. (For those that heaven't read it... <A HREF="http://www.anthrax.com" TARGET=_blank>www.anthrax.com</A>  Those guys never dreamed their band would share it's name with the major bull crap currently in the fan.)||||reg||1
